    "finding": "The area groups six named outlying island territories. DOC/UNESCO define five groups as New Zealand Subantarctic Islands (Snares, Bounty, Antipodes, Auckland, Campbell); Kermadec is a different, more northerly subtropical group. “Outlying islands” can describe the broad purpose, but is not equivalent to the strict subantarctic physical region. Five original sibling province packets share this area; assess all six together.",
    "proposal": "Leave all shared area memberships and boundaries unchanged. Coordinate review of all six member identities, the area tier and its distinction from other Southwest Pacific island groups."
  },
